<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Crusader Smyrna</h1><p class="st-meta">1344 CE – 1402 CE · capital Smyrna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Latin outpost in the harbour of Smyrna, seized by a crusade in 1344 and held by the Knights Hospitaller until Timur destroyed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>To stop the raids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umur-bey">Umur Bey</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aydinids">Aydinids</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-vi">Pope Clement VI</a> organised a naval league with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a>. In October 1344 its fleet captured the harbour castle of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/smyrna">Smyrna</a>, while the Turks kept the upper citadel on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-pagus">Mount Pagus</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony was a fortified enclave held by a mixed garrison under a papal captain, supplied by sea and constantly under pressure from the Turks above. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umur-bey">Umur Bey</a> was killed attacking it in 1348, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humbert-ii-of-viennois">Humbert II of Viennois</a> led a further expedition in 1345-1347. From 1374 the pope entrusted <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/smyrna">Smyrna</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Hospitallers</a>, who held it as an outpost of their state on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rhodes">Rhodes</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In December 1402 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> besieged the castle after defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a>. He took it within about two weeks and massacred the defenders who did not escape by sea, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> presence.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="crusader state, 1344 CE – 1402 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">crusader state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.45%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1344 CE – 1402 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Smyrna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Italian, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hospitaller Smyrna, Latin Smyrna</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1373&amp;focus=crusader-smyrna" aria-label="Crusader Smyrna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5355 798 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Crusader Smyrna lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5675 1054L5710 1120M5675 1054L6582 1190"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5710 1120h0M6582 1190h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5675 1054h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5675 1054h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Smyrna. <a href="/atlas?year=1373&amp;focus=crusader-smyrna">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

